In **Book of Genesis** 32, **Jacob** prepares to face his brother **Esau**, whom he deceived years earlier, and the fear of that encounter drives him to prayer and deep dependence on God. That night, alone by the **Jabbok**, Jacob wrestles with a mysterious man who reveals Himself to be God. Sometimes God must break us before He blesses us—but the limp we carry afterward is often the mark of His transforming grace.
